# Clean Code — Functions & Tests (R3)

**Craftsmanship = knowledge + practice.** Code is written for human readers.

## Functions

- **Small; do one thing** — One abstraction level per function; stepdown rule (read top-to-bottom).
- **Few arguments** — Prefer parameter objects over flag arguments; no hidden side effects.
- **Fail fast** — Validate preconditions early; return/throw immediately on invalid state.

## Tests (FIRST)

- **F**ast, **I**ndependent, **R**epeatable, **S**elf-validating, **T**imely
- One assert per concept; test code as clean as production code.
- **Learning tests** for third-party APIs you don't control.

## Error handling

- Use exceptions over error codes; don't return or pass null when avoidable.
- Wrap third-party APIs at boundaries (see R2).

## Boy Scout rule

Leave the code cleaner than you found it — small improvements in touched areas.

## Smell awareness (review)

